{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"48229c1ea3a5c0dfe4295a353cb4bbe8cb77acd847c456b6afe3aad15e6e1e2a","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira Cloud adapter backend factory","key_entities":["_build_jira_backend","resolve_jira_settings","AcliClient","BackendEnvError","JIRA_URL","JIRA_USER","JIRA_API_TOKEN","src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/backend.py","assert_transport_conforms","test_cloud_config_validation.py","test_transport_port_completeness_heldout.py"],"problem_keywords":["missing credentials","fail-fast validation","construction-time guard","email format validation","test parity","Cloud adapter","Jira backend"],"propositions":["_build_jira_backend constructs an AcliClient transport without validating that required credentials (JIRA_URL, JIRA_USER, JIRA_API_TOKEN) are present, allowing a wholly-unconfigured backend to build and fail only at first API call","Cloud adapter lacks the fail-fast construction-time credential guard present in DC adapter (which validates JIRA_PAT and raises BackendEnvError before transport construction)","JIRA_USER in Cloud requires an email address format but is not validated, causing silent Basic-auth failures with misleading 401 errors instead of clear config errors","Existing test test_cloud_build_backend_with_missing_credentials_does_not_fail_loudly documents the silent-build behavior as acceptable, creating a test-parity gap with DC's test_dc_pat_required_heldout.py"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787519279034904001,"uuid":"0175c287-0de3-4f27-aa45-b13cbfa8d3c2"}